{
 "nodes": [
  {
   "id": "cap-btitle",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -2200,
   "y": -420,
   "width": 1700,
   "height": 170,
   "text": "# Gemma 4 12B Unified — one decoder layer  \nLeft: the attention of the 40 **sliding** layers (224.1M per layer). Right: the 8 **full** layers (241.8M). A layer takes one of the two; norms, MLP, residuals are shared. Grey bars = tensors (0.05 px/channel, long ones clipped), boxes = operations with their weights."
  },
  {
   "id": "cap-blegend",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 800,
   "y": -420,
   "width": 1500,
   "height": 170,
   "text": "**Full layers save memory three ways**: one KV head (1 × 512) for all 16 query heads, **K = V** (no v_proj — keys and values are the same projection, normalised differently), and **p-RoPE** that rotates only 128 of 512 dims (θ 1,000,000), leaving the rest position-free for long range."
  },
  {
   "id": "xin1",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -96,
   "y": -180,
   "width": 192,
   "height": 9,
   "text": "",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
   "id": "note-lbl2",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 170,
   "y": -190,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 34,
   "text": "`x [T, 3840]  residual stream in`"
  },
  {
   "id": "n13",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -150,
   "y": -126,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 56,
   "text": "**input norm** — RMSNorm",
   "color": "3"
  },
  {
   "id": "h4",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -96,
   "y": -30,
   "width": 192,
   "height": 9,
   "text": "",
   "color": "#64748b"
  },
  {
