   "y": 2368,
   "width": 300,
   "height": 34,
   "text": "`x [T, 3840]  → next layer`"
  },
  {
   "id": "note-kv",
   "type": "text",
   "x": 2190,
   "y": 324,
   "width": 440,
   "height": 200,
   "text": "**KV cache per token** — sliding: K+V = 2 × 8 × 256 = 4,096 values, kept only for the last 1024 tokens. Full: K and V = 2 × 1 × 512 = 1,024 values for every token. K = V shares the weight, not the cached tensor: K gets k_norm + p-RoPE, V only a weightless RMSNorm."
  },
  {
   "id": "note-scale",
   "type": "text",
   "x": -2730,
   "y": 324,
   "width": 440,
   "height": 170,
   "text": "**qk-norm**: q and k are RMS-normalised per head with a learned weight, and the attention scale is 1 (no 1/√d). v is RMS-normalised without a weight. Same in both layer types."
  }
